The build checks the exact upstream Host and Client SHA-256 before applying
focused Antigravity retry/cooldown, Gemini system identity, quota UI compatibility,
Models settings integration, and package identity changes. Account storage, sign-in, token refresh, transport
and the other provider implementations retain the upstream implementation.
The upstream subscription package is a build input; the shipped Host and Client
contain the implementation and do not load that package at runtime.
Upstream upgrades require a reviewed rebuild; this enhancement does not claim
that arbitrary future upstream versions are compatible or automatically merged.

Version 0.2.1 additionally provides Host-only writing-mode model pairing and
category validation. It uses the pinned Cordis/Session pre-append dispatch
contract, with installed-runtime regression coverage, and leaves all native
Client selectors and transport permissions unchanged. Its writing composition is
copied from the DSH 0.2.2-rc.3 Minimal preset, replacing only its persona opener
with the user-approved Chinese writing identity. The MIT license of DSH
is retained in LICENSE-DSH. The Models extension uses provider-row styles
adapted from the same DSH release. No account data is included.

